I updated from RH-5.1 to RH-5.2 last night. The process was quite
smooth, but some problems were encountered:

* The update asks for the boot-disk, which I hadn't created, since I 
  booted from disk. But it was possible to create it on the fly by
  using the second virtual console.

* Obviously, the time during installation was twenty years off
  (2018). This didn't effect much files that were installed, but the
  directories touched and created in the process. To avoid this, you 
  should try to set the date on an alternate virtual console before
  the update utility actually installs the new packages.

* After the system went up again, it wasn't possible to mount the
  cdrom drive with 'mount /mnt/cdrom'.  It turned out that 'mount' was
  confused by an 'ignore' entry in /etc/fstab. Moving the cdrom entry
  in front of the ignored partition's entry solved this.

Other than that, I encounterd no problems so far. I allready
succesfully compiled qt-1.40 with it.

Martin
