> RAMDISK: Ext2 filesystem found at block 0
> RAMDISK: Loading 900 blocks into ram disk... done.
                   ^^^^^^^^^^
There's your trouble...

> VFS: Mounted root (ext2 filesystem) readonly.
> Unable to open an initial console.
> ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

The problem is that you were reading in the *boot* filesystem rather
than the *root* filesystem into ramdisk.  You should have a *separate*
ramdisk floppy (created from ramdisk.img).  After you've booted, you
switch out the boot disk and put in the ramdisk image.

If you don't get prompted to "insert the ramdisk floppy and hit ENTER",
then add "prompt_ramdisk=1" to the boot line.

If the RAMDISK message says you're loading 900 blocks, you've got
the wrong disk.  If it says you're loading 1400 or so blocks, you've
got the right one.

