A previous poster mentioned that you could get 8x36 true parity SIMMs from
www.multimediamemory.com (an outfit called "Discount Memory Products".) for $36
each.  While it's true that they do advertise this price on their web site,
when I called to ask about buying some, they mention that the price is now $84
per SIMM.  (Which is actually quite a bit higher than even cpumicromart's
price).  Bottom line- forget about these guys.  If their web site is *that* our
of date, who knows when you'd actually get your memory?  Not to mention that it
took three tries before someone answered the phone.

So, can anyone recommend a good source for true parity SIMMs?  I'm considering
ordering from Dynasty Express again, but I was wondering if there was a cheaper
source.  KDE needs RAM. :)

