Brian Wood said:
> I can say that AbiWord does compile and run on my 164SX running RH5.0 with the
> egcs compiler. As stated it is in an early state of development but looks good
> and has a lot of potential. I was very pleased that the developers very quickly
> responded to some Alpha-specific issues I raised, most such projects don't want
> to talk to you if you're not running Linux on an Intel.

Yeah, I was the guy who merged the Makefile stuff.  So far we've had
interest from Solaris, PPCLinux, and Alpha Linux users (besides the
big Intel).  I've been on the axp-linux list for a whole 2 days now,
and had I known Brian was here, too, I'd have named him in my first post. :)

Back to AbiWord, we're making lots of progress on it.  I will probably commit
some font changes soon so that one can use real fonts (with some, not all,
X font properties recognized/stored).  Clipboard and printing are still
coming; the formatter and GUI are steadily moving along.  These features
should round out the M1 list.  You can view the spec database through
our web site.  We'll have Bugzilla up shortly so people can use a quick
forms interface to submit problems.

Also, I might as well take some time here to ask about Alpha hardware
(which I'm wanting to buy).  Basically, I've got about $2200 I want
to spend on just an Alpha chip and a motherboard, since most (all?)
of my current hardware _should_ work well with the new guts.  My
hard drive is SCSI (IBM UltraStar 9ZX) off a BusLogic BT-958 SCSI-3
(or whatever they call UW SCSI-2 with those extensions); my video
card is a PCI Matrox Millennium II, and I've got two ISA sound cards
(those can go if I need to buy a PCI sound card).  There's some more
SCSI stuff on that chain, and I've got a 3Dfx I don't expect to work
(unless there are Alpha Linux GLIDE drivers).  

I've been looking at the 164LX boards, but are the 164UXes nicer?
Also, should I just put this off for a few more months and either
get a 21264 I can afford or buy a 21164 really cheap (when they
cut prices)?  I'm right now basing prices off dcginc.com's 
systems at http://www.dcginc.com/97/linuxlx.htm.

DCG LX Series 21164a-533MHz Digital Alpha (NT/L LX-1)
2MB 3rd Level Synchronous SRAMS Cache, 9ns 
1.44mb Sony floppy
