Have to ask. What is the fastest Intel you use?

To be fair, I suggest you use the same drive/
adapter for test comparisons. I suspect your
Alpha is faster due to those particular parts
more than it is the Alpha itself. 

On the other hand, for my code tests, my 533LX
is significantly faster than my PII 400. Also,
my RS/6000/397 is faster than the 533LX. Note
I'm not looking at price/performance here, only
raw performance, on my own tests, which are 
always the best way for a company to judge a
machine for their own use. The usual YMMV
clause applies.

I use external benchmarks like SPEC and Linpack
to decide what machines I'm interested in testing
and then try to get access to the short list for
testing purposes. Worst case, I buy one to see
what it can do. That's not so bad because then
I have another platform to cross test my code on.
For your average hobbyist, that may not work so 
well.


