Subject:	S3d Virge GX2 on AlphaStation 500/266


Dear All,

I just got a new graphics card which is a S3d Virge GX2 noname product. >I 
try
to run it on an AlphaStation 500/266 aka Alcor. The system is running with 
a
plain S3 Trio64V. I am running kernel 2.0.30.

On a RH-5.1 system + all relevant 5.1 updates I start XConfigurator to 
setup
the card, it recognizes it correctly, installs the XFree86_S3V server and 
the
configuration is fine.
Starting X -probeonly works ok, running X crashes the machine completely.

Configuring it using xf86config recognizes it as well but is using the SVGA
server ( which is supposed to work as well on this card ).
Still, in the end it comes down to the same result - complet system crash !

Any hints ?

Greetings,
Jochen
