> In the case of the generation of Alpha you are mentioning (21066) they had
> a few good qualtities in pipelines, cache, and so forth, so I would equate
> this to be more a case of divide by 1.66. In other words it runs integer
> about like a P100.

In my experience this is largely dependent on cache size.  A low end
multia is more like a P75, maybe worse.  My AS200 4/233 is comparable
to a P133.

