> > list, it is a problem with ncurses.
> 
> Are you sure?  I have seen that with other programs and this was a
> portability bug in a sources.  Wrong terminal model.  Actually simple
> patches for RasMol, which I posted on this list a while ago, were solving
> **exactly** that anonyance.
> 
> The other know samples of that behaviour were ispell from 5.0 and 5.1
> (only in a terminal mode, not when called from another program -
> not anymore in 'rawhide' so I guess also not in 5.2) and metamail.

The bug lies in the curses emulation mode of ncurses.  If you compile a
program that directly uses ncurses, it doesn't have a problem, but *any*
program that uses curses, and finds ncurses libraries will have it...

I'd love to see this fixed...anyone want to submit a patch to the ncurses
maintainers?

-- Bob

