On Fri, 6 Nov 1998, Paul Tomblin wrote:

> Quoting axp-list@duct.ml.org (axp-list@duct.ml.org):
> > Out of curiosity...  can these TV cards achieve full screen video?  even
> > on say 1600x1200?
> 
> Isn't an NTSC video signal about 600x400 or something like that?  How would
> you make a tv picture bigger without it looking blocky?

With a sufficiently fast computer or dedicated processor you could
theoretically smooth every frame. Smoothing does distort the image a
bit, but at a reasonable frame rate you wouldn't notice it. If in fact
the NTSC signal is 600x400ish, I suspect that one could scale this up
to 800x600 with little trouble.. of course, smoothing is CPU intensive
so you'd need either a custom chip, or maybe a programmable DSP could
pull it off. 

Michael J. Graffam (mgraffam@idsi.net)


