>
>I've run  my 2940UW with 2.0.33-2.0.35 kernels compiled against egcs 1.1b and
>just recently I've attached a scsi zip and it works fine. They only time I've
>ever had  a problem with this card is when I was playing with some early E
0.15
>CVS stuff and esound did something to the scsi bus that froze the system and
>took it down.  Also my card is very old, I  bought it from a computer show
and
>found drivers for NT 3.5 in there. It originally had 2.23 bios and now has a 
>2.25 bios. My point is if you plan to get an adaptec try to get an older one.
>Though with the introduction of the 2.2 kerenls it shouldn't matter how
old the
>card is and these problems others are experencing should disapear. 
>
A lot of the problems I have seen on these cards is when you leave enabled
the "auto-termination" function in the BIOS. Often, disabling this, and
manually enabling or disabling it makes things work better. Also, as with
any SCSI setup, Adaptec, or otherwise, using good quality active
terminators often makes things work much more reliably.


