Component vendors covers a lot for example:
  1) Component vendors who know about Linux
  2) Component vendors who know about Linux/Alpha (e.g. video cards are
more limited than Intel?)
  3) Component vendors who know about Alpha
  4) Component vendors who spell specific useful things - e.g. RAM which
     is known to work on Alpha

Perhaps the answer is not to categories but instead to put them down in
name/geographical order in a table with a column for each of the
attributes (linux, Alpha, Systems, tech support, components, Compaq
components, penguins) with ticks in the columns (or perhaps one of
'-' for no, C for claimed, Y for yes (someone has reported them having
met the attribute).

