True, they have no memory and are underpowered for many environments.
But, they have significant CoolFactor (tm).  I was thinking about
assembling a small Beowulf with my AS200, and a couple of these Multias.
Mostly to experiment with parallelism, but I would actually be able to use
it for a project.  Also, I was considering using one in my audio system as
a MP3 player, pulling stuff off of my main system with a lot more disk
space via 10BT.  Low profile, low power, low cost.  Mostly, it would just
be a pretty cool toy to have around.  I am a geek, and this is how I have
fun.  That and Quake.  



