Hello

As far as your memory is concern, in your manual there is description of
what type of memory you need.  However alpha's are very picky about
memory, even if your specification is exactly correct, it still might
not work.  The best solution I can tell you is either get memory that
has been alpha certified or to get in through us.

Video cards... well that depends what you planning to do with it.
S3 video chipset is probably the most common (i.e. diamond  )
Metrox is very common cards
The best? That is hard to say I am not sure which one I would chose as
the best.  The one that we sell the most is a keyvision card.  Its based
on S3 video chipset its very chip and simple card, but its what most
Linux users want.

Those are the most common cards that we use, and I would go with those
unless you have some special purpose in mind for them (i.e. need very
good resolution)
As far as what other cards are supported the best way to look at is at
this URL: http://www.xfree86.org/3.3.2/README3.html
<http://www.xfree86.org/3.3.2/README3.html>  
This tells you all the chipsets that are supported.  Also there is a
file /usr/X11R6/lib/X11/Cards
That tells you all the cards that are supported.  Not that it matters
these days since all video cards are pretty much PCI, but you want to
make sure that you get PCI card.  ISA buss is not quiet right on the LX
board.  In other words something's don't quiet work


Well hope this helps
Marek Dohojda
Carrera Computers, inc.


