On Mon, 9 Nov 1998, Nicholas Sallembian wrote:

> Hi all,
> 
> I have installed RedHat 5.1 on my Multia very recently, it was my first
> experience with Linux/Alpha, and without counting the time it took to
...
> Secondly, I would like to recompile my kernel. I grabbed the latest
> sources from kernel.org, and untarred everything. I set ARCH = alpha in
> the top level Makefile, and set the symbolic links to the correct asm
> directory, but I can't start anything, even make config does not work,
> it just says arch/alpha is a directory. Is there something to do that I
> am not doing ?

Actually, there's something you ARE doing that you shouldn't be.  There is
no need to set the ARCH in the toplevel Makefile, and you should never need
to manually make symlinks (there is a separate target in the Makefile for
that, that gets automatically run at the proper times).  Just untar your
kernel and run "make config dep clean boot modules".  Depending on the
kernel version, you may need to patch in the latest Alpha-specific
bugfixes, available somewhere on gatekeeper.dec.com.

cheers,
-bp
