    Wai-Sun> which defines a variable with the name as "i386" ought to be
    Wai-Sun> shot, but "alpha" is a pretty common variable. This is
    Wai-Sun> especially so in the graphics world where there is such a
    Wai-Sun> thing as an alpha-channel: in fact if you were to do a
    Wai-Sun> recursive grep in the WindowMaker sources, you'd be swamped!

