> Well...  I have just discovered that even though there are fixes
> available, Red Hat 5.2 for alpha *still* includes the XF86_SVGA binary
> that wont let you open more than 20-25 windows.  With all the carelessness
> I have been seeing in recent months with the 5.x series, I am led to
> wonder if Red Hat actually has QA department...

	The fix has been available since June 1998, but it hasn't
	even made it thru XFree86 base release work.  The fix is
	rather widely affecting thing that reworks basic X11 server's
	socket select() facilities, and as such it has had serious
	fears of causing problem in other places.   DEC UNIX has
	also problems due to this very same X11 basic code.

	It is quite rare to run X server so that it has more than
	those fine working 32 sockets active, therefore  RH QA  has
	very likely missed this case (and the X11 community as well..)

	If you want working XF86_SVGA binary, pick my oldish
	  ftp://mea.tmt.tele.fi/pub/XFree86/XF86_SVGA.alpha.bin.gz

