On Wed, 11 Nov 1998, Wai-Sun Chia wrote:

> Then I tried to do the same thing with my AS200 at the office, but I
> couldn't find any equivalents. I even tried to put "VGA=ask" at the MILO
> prompt, which was ignored...

If you have a true TGA "E"-series video controller in your Alpha, there is
no VGA support of any kind.  The "VGA=" line will mean nothing.

> Any one successfully tried a FB bigger than 640x480 on the Alpha with
> the TGA card?

According to the Frambuffer-HOWTO, the TGA framebuffer only supports one
resolution.

---

9. Using framebuffer devices on Alpha platforms                        

9.1 What modes are available to me?             

   So far, there is only the TGA PCI card - which only does 80x30 with a 
   resolution of 640x480 at either 8 bits or 24/32 bits.
                                                                         
9.2 Which graphic cards can work with the frambuffer device?
     
   This lists all the graphic cards that are known to work:

     * DEC TGA PCI (DEC21030) - 640x480 @ 8 bit or 24/32 bit versions

---

I'd like to see this change, too.  But I've personally had little time and
knowledge to invest in it. :)

-bp
