The CDROMs are ISO9660 compliant, and you can mount them on a Wintel PC and
look in the directories for the files needed to make the disks. The first
floppyis a FAT16 filecopy operation for MILO and LINLOAD.EXE. The second is
a floppy image you make using RAWRITE.EXE

Instructions and filesa are on the CDROMs.

Does you vendor not provide Linux support? By the name "Durango" I gather
you have purchased LX based systems from Aspen. Their number is (303)
431-4606.

BTW, Greg Lindahl, is this OK?


