Tanking your loader will certainly cause you big grief.  I would imagine
it's much easier to repair the situation while the system is still running,
because your shell is already linked and loaded and you could use some of
the few statically linked tools available** to (possibly) fix the situation.
My advice is to boot off a rescue disk; the one you used to install your
box should suffice.

**on my RedHat-5.1 Alpha box:

% foreach i ( `ls -1 /{s,}bin/*` )
. if( {(file $i|&grep -q "ELF .* executable")} ) then
. (ldd $i|&grep -q "not a dynamic") && echo $i is statically linked
. endif
. end
/bin/ash.static is statically linked
/bin/rpm is statically linked
/sbin/e2fsck is statically linked
/sbin/fsck.ext2 is statically linked
/sbin/insmod.static is statically linked
/sbin/ldconfig is statically linked
/sbin/rmmod.static is statically linked
/sbin/sln is statically linked
% 

cheers,
-bp
