Not entirely inert.  Gold has no native oxide, yes.  Gold corrodes very,
very slowly, yes, although I think faster than diamonds devolve to an
ordinary lump of carbon. Tin, though does have a native oxide, and it does
corrode.  Therefore, there is some concern there.  If you want to slap
some RAM and not worry about ever taking the case apart, there may be
some concern, but I usually take computer cases apart once per year to
cast out the dust anyways.

Another question: for the electronic contacts in a computer, would using
a little silicone grease affect the life of the parts or corrosion either
way?

