Hmmm...I did a fresh install of the the 4.5 x86 netscape binaries,
loaded up all the em86 stuff, copied the script (as below) and went
for it.  Up came NetCenter.  I punched in www.news.com and got about
halfway through their splash.  Then it pretty much locked (NS 4.5, not
the whole box and not X).  I had top running on it from another host,
and netscape was chewing up about 97.something % of my cpu and a
metric boatload of ram.  There were a handful of unaligned trap errors
in /var/log/messages, but I thought the current wisdom was to pretty
much ignore them.  I tried this both as root and non-root, FWIW.
 
Here's the pertinents:
Box: 	 AS200 4/233 (Avanti), RH5.1
Ram: 	 80M
Swap: 	160M
Kernel: 2.0.34
X:	3.3.2-13 (S3 server)
Disk:	more than enough for the next month, with all due respect to Ken Thompson :)

Between the time it loaded and the time it locked, it ran very well!
If anybody's made any progress on these issues, please post or mail me.
TIA,
-ls-

