Mime-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"


This is just a quick note for everyone that had problems with that funky
overflow in klogd.  With a duct-tape fix in the kernel by adding a '\n' in
the src does not totally fix the problem, and there is updated code.  

Some notes from Martin Schulze (current maintainer):

> from klogd man page (1.3)
> <-snip->
>   AUTHOR
> The klogd was originally written by Steve Lord (lord@cray.com), Greg
> Wettstein made major improvements.
>        Dr. Greg Wettstein (greg@wind.rmcc.com)
>        Enjellic Systems Development
> <-snip->
>>
>>Hmm, you're right, there were several references to Greg's old address
>>left over.  I'll change it with the next version.
>>Please take a look at the current source, you'll find Greg's new address
>>at greg@wind.enjellic.com.
>
> Where is the point of origin for all of ths syslogd & klogd source ?
>
>>This is currently - as stated in the source, but not in the .lsm by my
>>mistake - ftp://ftp.infodrom.north.de/pub/people/joey/sysklogd/

According to Martin, the new code is fixed and should not have the overflow
problems as did the older version.  Yet, the new code is NOT added into
most Linux distros, and until just a few weeks ago I think Redhat 5.2 just
came out with some Errata....

<snip>
Package: Sysklogd 
Updated: 17-Nov-1998 

Problem: 

(17-Nov-1998):Security Fix 
A buffer overflow has been identified in all versions of the sysklogd
packages shipped with Red Hat Linux. As the time of this post there are no
known exploits for this security vulnerability. 

(found by axp-list a long long time ago.. just had to add this)
Red Hat would like to thank Michal Zalewski (lcamtuf@IDS.PL) and the
members of the Bugtraq mailing list for discovering this problem and
providing a fix. 

Users of Red Hat Linux are recommended to upgrade to the new packages
available under updates directory on our ftp site: 

Solution: 

Intel: Upgrade to: 
sysklogd-1.3-26 
Alpha: Upgrade to: 
sysklogd-1.3-26 
<-snip->


Well everyone take it easy..

-Barrett


