When you rawrite the images to floppies (or dd) linload will be created on
the milo disk.  The image is actually a full DOS disk and needs to be
written to a floppy to use it (1.44 MB)-- in fact, all of these .img files
need to be prepared by writing them out to a disk -- not copying them onto
the disk; the images aren't just files, they are whole filesystems.  Check
out the install info on the dec multia info page on www.cpumicromart.com
-- it's the best quick get-you-up-and-going multia howto that I've found.
(click on the multia info thing on the front page and then look for the
links on the bottom of the next page).

-Tymm

